      "summary": ": Today at CARDRONA ALPINE RESORT 30 Aug 2026 – \"10:00am Update: Due to no decrease in winds across the mountain, all lifts will now be closed for the day. The Learners Slope Conveyors will remain open until 1pm. We will be open today but we currently have strong westerly winds that may impact our chairlift operations throughout the day - It's a day for the enthusiasts! The forecast is for snow showers down to 900m throughout the day, and strong Westerly winds. The snowpack has dried out more but we still have firm conditions across the mountain. This will create some variable conditions, particularly off-piste, so we ask everyone to take care when venturing off the groomed trails. The Main Basin is scheduled to open at 08:30am, Captains and T-Bar will follow from 09:00am wind allowing. Soho and Willows are currently On-Hold until wind and snow pack assessments have been completed. Road Status: The Road is Chainfree but we are expecting a Chain call this morning so Chains must be carried. Ride Tribe / Academy / Mini will be cancelled today.\"",
