      "summary": ": Today at TREBLE CONE 30 Aug 2026 – \"Open! - We're stoked to be back at it and welcoming all of you back to the mountain! After some wild weather and a fair bit of work to tidy up in its wake we're back on track. Although we did pick up a descent hit of snow (70cm) it then rained on top of that which made for some spicy conditions across the mountain. A few days of letting that moisture drain out has left us with good coverage of snow that is skiing well with a bit of a crust on top, that coupled with plenty of grooming should make for some great skiing and riding across the mountain. We've worked hard over the last few days to get the mountain tidied up after the storm, but please be aware that we haven't been open for a few days and there may be some unmarked hazards out there - spend a bit of time exploring and find where the good stuff is before sending it too hard! Weather - The forecast today is for some snow showers and strong winds with a lowering freezing level; we've just seen those winds picking up; The Saddle Basin is ON HOLD Ride Tribe is on today, we're pumped to see ya'll up here! Access road - although our teams have worked hard clearing debris and damage from the road there are a few random piles of debris and large rocks in few locations on the side of the road, there's also some water damage to some edges of the road. As a result, a few sections are slightly narrower now so take care. If you're the type to get antsy behind a slow vehicle, today might be the day to just chill out and just follow the car in front of you; you'll all arrive in the same place at roughly the same time anyway. Just be safe!\"",
